<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria M1 falls 6.15 pct,M2 off 2.55 pct in week.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria M1 falls 6.15 pct,M2 off 2.55 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian M1 money supply fell to 706.6 billion levs on May 30 from 752.9 billion levs a week earlier and M2 decreased to 3,307.8 billion levs from 3,394.4 billion levs, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Total broad money fell 2.35 percent to 3,491.8 billion levs in the week to May 30.</p>
<p>Conversion of dollar-denominated deposits into levs was made at the central bank fixings of 1,568.1 levs per dollar for May 30, 1,566.8 for May 23 and 1,467.8 for April 25.</p>
